      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Replication steps: \n*  Go to world with stream player while audio is set to 48000Hz. \n*  Play a random twitch stream; audio should play. \n*  Change audio sample rate to 44100 Hz for your audio device.\n*  Try playing the stream again (probably needs a re-launch of VRCHat because audio device changed) \n*  No audio from stream. \nTo change audio sample rate (Windows 10): \n* Right click audio speakers in taskbar -> Open Sound Settings \n* CLick \"Sound Control Panel\" on top right under Related Settings\n* Find your audio device, right click, go to Properties\n* Change sample rate under \"Default Format\" on the \"Advanced Tab\"",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-04-06T14:42:11.544Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Tested with VRC_Stream Sync and VRChat 2020.1.1p1 (Build 916)\n\nIf your audio device is set to sampling rate of 44100 Hz the videos that have 44100 Hz Audio won't play said Audio. However it will play 48000 Hz Audio\n\n48000 Hz Devices will play both 44100 Hz Audio and 48000 Hz Audio",
